(FIL-36: a numeric at is a borrowed descriptor - the handle reports exactly the number written; FIL-43: 0 and 2147483647 are accepted.
 Also covers: FIL-43, and FIL-80 for the dead descriptor (a write and a read
 on 2147483647 set the error flag). Rendered shapes of 'gen leaf file
 borrowed descriptors'; descriptor 1 writes its marker straight into
 this output.
 Run from the vox-fuzz worktree root; the probe creates everything it
 needs under vf_scratch/files/ and touches nothing else.
 Ran (vox 0.4.15, 2026-10-05): VOX_CORE_PATH=/usr/share/vox/coreasm /usr/bin/vox docs/ledger/probes/files/FIL-36.vox -o p && printf 'hello world, this is the input\nsecond line\n' | ./p
 exit code 0; actual output:
   2147483647
   1
   2147483647
   1
   0
   1
   ptba5l82a6
   0
)
